{"id":55,"text":"It was a stormy night, and the Millers were having dinner when somebody knocked on the door. Mrs. Miller opened it and saw a tired old man in a wet coat.\n\n“I’m sorry to disturb you,” he said. “My car has broken down, and there are no hotels nearby. Could I stay by your fire until the morning?”\n\nMr. Miller hesitated. They didn’t know the man. But he looked harmless, and the weather was terrible. “Come in,” he said finally.\n\nThey gave him hot soup and a warm blanket. The old man was very polite. He told them stories about his travels and made their children laugh. By midnight, they were all friends.\n\nIn the morning, the storm had passed. The man thanked them and walked out to the road. A few minutes later, a car arrived. Two men in suits jumped out and hurried to him. “Sir, we have been looking for you all night!”\n\nMrs. Miller was surprised. “Who is he?” she whispered to her husband.\n\nA week later, they received a letter. It was from the old man, who was the owner of a large company. Inside was a cheque and a short note: “Thank you for opening your door when you did not need to.”\n\nMoral: Kindness to strangers is never a waste.","tr":null,"gl":{"it":"u (narsa)","was":"edi","a":"bir (noaniq artikl)","stormy":"bo'ronli","night":"tun, kecha","and":"va","the":"(aniq artikl)","millers":"tegirmonchilar","were":"edi(lar)","having":"ega bo'lish","dinner":"kechki ovqat","when":"qachon; -ganda","somebody":"kimdir","knocked":"taqillatdi","on":"ustida, -da","door":"eshik","mrs":"xonim","miller":"tegirmonchi","opened":"ochdi","saw":"ko'rdi","tired":"charchagan","old":"keksa, eski","man":"odam, kishi","in":"ichida, -da","wet":"ho'l","coat":"palto","i'm":"men ... -man","sorry":"kechirasiz, afsus","to":"-ga; uchun","disturb":"bezovta qilmoq","you":"sen, siz","he":"u (erkak)","said":"dedi","my":"mening","car":"mashina","has":"bor","broken":"singan","down":"pastga","there":"u yerda; bor","are":"-dir, -siz, -lar (to be)","no":"yo'q; hech qanday","hotels":"m